      "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: an opaque full-frame high-definition replacement for the actual 64x64/66x64 WOOD37 shared rolling-wood and falling-rock spell movie in a historical Three Kingdoms strategy game. Create one square, complete scene with no margins; every edge is filled with the environment. This is one of two alternating original native picture slots, not a sprite sheet. Match a restrained, richly textured painted game-art style: weathered gray-brown rock, warm sandstone highlights, muted olive-black shadows and dusty earth, fine hand-painted natural detail. The native image shows rocky mountains and tumbling stones; preserve that subject rather than adding logs or interpreting the skill name as a new scene. Three angular mountain crags fill the upper half: the left peak is highest near the upper-left quarter, a smaller central crag slopes diagonally down to the center, and the right crag rises along the right edge. A sloping rocky ledge runs across the middle, with a nearer dusty foreground in the bottom half. Several separate irregular dark-edged boulders fall and tumble diagonally downward toward the viewer, with short dust trails, readable large silhouettes and spaces between them. Use a locked slightly elevated frontal viewpoint. No people, horses, buildings, magic symbols, text, letters, border, watermark, interface, or unrelated props. No transparent areas: fully opaque scenic painting. At the game's small logical display the three crags and moving stones must remain clear. Picture slot 0: an earlier falling-stone pose. Put a conspicuous falling boulder below the left peak in the upper-left-middle, another around the center-left ledge, one in the mid-right, and scattered smaller nearer stones across lower-left, lower-center and lower-right. Dust remains subdued. The bottom-center boulder is relatively small and close to the lower edge.",
